\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Matched contrast at caliper $.25$ on three configuration sets. The first two rows are the with-and-without comparison the deviation log committed to before the grid was scored. The augmented set pools two populations --- 30 of its 51 pairs lie entirely inside the extended $\gamma $ regime --- so the third row, which requires each pair to touch an originally registered configuration, isolates the like-for-like subset; that row was defined after the grid was run and is post hoc. Matching is blind to seed, so a pair may span two of them; intervals are the multiway cluster bootstrap, which admits a pair only when both of its seeds are drawn.}}{18}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:support}{{8}{18}{Matched contrast at caliper $.25$ on three configuration sets. The first two rows are the with-and-without comparison the deviation log committed to before the grid was scored. The augmented set pools two populations --- 30 of its 51 pairs lie entirely inside the extended $\gamma $ regime --- so the third row, which requires each pair to touch an originally registered configuration, isolates the like-for-like subset; that row was defined after the grid was run and is post hoc. Matching is blind to seed, so a pair may span two of them; intervals are the multiway cluster bootstrap, which admits a pair only when both of its seeds are drawn}{table.8}{}}
